  "schemaVersion": "openclinxr.parent-fitted-teeth.silhouette-seat.v1",
  "instrument": "Arch face: row membership is base Y, clear of the teeth Y median by 0.006 m. Each 2 mm world-x bin keeps verts within 2 mm of that bin's world max z. Lead is tooth world z minus the max z of body verts within 6 mm in x and y, after applyVisemeWeights at weight 1 and applyJawOpenToRoot. Positive lead means the crown is in front of that skin. Missing means no body vert in the window; those verts are excluded from the max. Band maxMm is rounded to 0.001 mm; null means no arch-face vert in that world |x| band.",
  "references": {
    "lowerOpening": "jaw-descendant skin. Clause is viseme_aa, viseme_E, viseme_I, viseme_O, viseme_U. Limit -0.0005 m.",
    "upper": "any body vert. Clause is viseme_aa, viseme_E, viseme_I, viseme_O, viseme_U, viseme_FF, viseme_PP. Limit < 0.",
    "closed": "any body vert, both rows. Clause is viseme_PP and viseme_sil. Limit -0.010 m."
  },
